WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.629 --> 00:00:07.430
The Pawn Stars from the World Famous Gold
and Silver Pawn Shop on the Las Vegas strip

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:08.880
seem to know it all.

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.290
From muskets to coins, autographs to automobiles,
the team has the cash and charisma to woo

00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:16.049
customers and TV audiences from around the
world.

00:00:16.049 --> 00:00:20.839
But success in business doesn't mean perfection,
and sometimes even the best get bamboozled.

00:00:20.839 --> 00:00:24.439
In a History Channel segment in 2010, Rick
Harrison discussed the time he was cheated

00:00:24.439 --> 00:00:25.439
by a girl's best friend.

00:00:25.439 --> 00:00:29.249
A man in a sharp suit was looking to pawn
a pair of diamond earrings.

00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:32.590
Harrison asked all the right questions, and
the seller gave all the right answers—and

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.899
even had a receipt.

00:00:33.899 --> 00:00:35.350
Harrison forked over $40,000.

00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.790
But three days later, the police showed up.

00:00:37.790 --> 00:00:41.800
Apparently, he'd actually bought some hot
diamonds, or in other words: stolen goods.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:45.780
The victim got her diamonds back and the criminal
paid the price, but Harrison was out his $40K.

00:00:45.780 --> 00:00:49.040
"That was the biggest bust I ever had in the
pawn shop," he said.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.640
Richard "The Old Man" Harrison says fake diamonds
have swindled him the most.

00:00:52.640 --> 00:00:56.720
When cubic zirconia, a synthetic diamond doppelgänger,
first hit the market in the seventies and

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.640
eighties, plenty of pawn shops were duped.

00:00:58.640 --> 00:01:01.160
"Nobody knew about them, and they tested as
diamonds.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:04.030
Everybody in the industry bought a bunch of
them," said Harrison in 2010.

00:01:04.030 --> 00:01:07.100
He said he wasted nearly $30,000.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:10.240
But these days, cubic zirconias don't pose
as much of a problem.

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:14.579
The Old Man's grandson, Corey "Big Hoss" Harrison,
even filmed a video for the History Channel

00:01:14.579 --> 00:01:17.630
in 2009 called, "How to Spot a Fake Diamond."

00:01:17.630 --> 00:01:21.630
Corey said that the fake rocks are "too perfect,"
adding that "There are very, very few perfect

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.630
diamonds out there."

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:24.930
So the seller on the street probably doesn't
own one.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:28.749
He recommends examining gems under a magnifying
glass or asking a reputable jeweler to take

00:01:28.749 --> 00:01:30.049
a closer look.

00:01:30.049 --> 00:01:33.350
Though Corey grew up in the pawn shop, he
had to learn some business lessons the hard

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.350
way.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.149
The Big Hoss explained: "When I first started
working the night shift, I didn't have that

00:01:37.149 --> 00:01:40.810
much experience here, and being the typical
18-year-old kid, I thought I knew everything.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:45.069
It must have got around town pretty quick
because I bought six fake Rolexes in one week."

00:01:45.069 --> 00:01:48.729
His foolhardy ways cost him four-grand...and
really ticked off his family.

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:52.409
Viewers have learned there are thousands of
tricks that sellers use on fake timepieces.

00:01:52.409 --> 00:01:56.799
Corey's dad, Rick Harrison, shared some time-tested
tips in a 2009 segment, but his bottom line

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:00.630
was this: "If you're going to buy a Rolex
off somebody…don't buy it off the internet.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:01.810
Don't buy it off Craigslist.

00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:04.979
Come to a guy like me if you want a used one,
or go buy a new one.

00:02:04.979 --> 00:02:06.299
Don't buy it off the street."

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:07.299
Thanks for watching!

00:02:07.299 --> 00:02:08.509
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to see more
videos like the one you just saw.

